# Bug: `Context.Scheme()` accepts invalid forwarded scheme values (missing validity check)

## 1. Pristine source (`git show HEAD:context.go` — /echo/context.go lines 252–271)
```go
252: func (c *context) Scheme() string {
253: 	// Can't use `r.Request.URL.Scheme`
254: 	// See: https://groups.google.com/forum/#!topic/golang-nuts/pMUkBlQBDF0
255: 	if c.IsTLS() {
256: 		return "https"
257: 	}
258: 	if scheme := c.request.Header.Get(HeaderXForwardedProto); scheme != "" {
259: 		return scheme
260: 	}
261: 	if scheme := c.request.Header.Get(HeaderXForwardedProtocol); scheme != "" {
262: 		return scheme
263: 	}
264: 	if ssl := c.request.Header.Get(HeaderXForwardedSsl); ssl == "on" {
265: 		return "https"
266: 	}
267: 	if scheme := c.request.Header.Get(HeaderXUrlScheme); scheme != "" {
268: 		return scheme
269: 	}
270: 	return "http"
271: }
```
There is **no** `isValidScheme`/`validScheme` helper anywhere in the package (`grep -rn 'isValidScheme\|validScheme' /echo` → nothing). Header constants are in echo.go:203–206 and are correct.

## 2. Existing tests
`/echo/context_test.go:746–802` `TestContext_Scheme` is table-driven with only valid values (TLS, XFP https, XFProtocol http, XFSsl on, XUrlScheme https, empty) and **no invalid-value cases**, so it passes on the buggy code (`cd /echo && go test .` → `ok`). The hidden test adds subtests for invalid values, which the current code cannot pass.

## 3. Root cause
Lines 258, 261, 267 only test `scheme != ""`. Any non-empty value (`ftp`, `gopher`, `garbage`, …) is returned verbatim as the scheme instead of being ignored/falling through. (Line 264's `X-Forwarded-Ssl == "on"` check is fine.)

